e friends  don't believe it it is something that  only he seems to believe yeah and yet  though Crimea is still part of Russian  territory and these troops aren't the  troops that are going immediately now to  Ukraine these new conscripts some of  them with no training whatsoever some of  them with two or three weeks with no  equipment I was looking at some material  last night where they were being told  get hold of sanitary pads from your  wives and your mothers because they're  the best we've got for bandages because  they will absorb blood bring your bring  their first aid kits out of your cars we  can't give you any these people are  being sent with literally nothing but a  uniform and a rifle to the front now  they're not going to be there to fight  the Russians are defending they're  digging in right round the front and so  if they bring in these new conscripts  just to hold a piece of front which is  easier than really fighting then they  can release some of the troops who've  been there for eight months without a  break to rotate them get them back into  some areas where they can reorganize  them give them a bit of rest and so on  so the the logic for bringing these new  completely untrained recruits to the  front is to take experienced soldiers  away from the front so they can  reorganize for what will be I'm fairly  sure a big Russian counter-offensive  next year after the winter they're  digging in for the winter when the  weather starts to break again in  February March then we can expect the  Russians to push then to a really big  probably a nationwide offensive and the  ukrainians and the West will have to be  ready for that just a final thought  would Ukraine not have expected Europe  and the West to have stepped in to try  to stop these referenda going ahead uh  no the there's nothing you can do about  the referendum there's nothing the West  can do without getting directly involved  so in a way what the West has done is  all it can do is to say thi